<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Stands in for the target's layout/probe.xml once the resource replacement is installed.

    Three things in here are payload, and each is read by a different part of the framework.

    android:tag needs no rewriting at all; it is what says whose document was inflated.

    The two id references are the value half of the rewrite. Both are compiled as this package's own
    ids, so the framework has to translate them before the app inflates the document. probe_root is
    the one the case reads back: the target declares that name too, so it has to come back as the
    target's number. module_only is here for the numbering below, and the fake 0x7e id it turns into
    - it exists in no other package - is not asserted anywhere: whether an unresolvable reference
    survives the inflater's TypedArray is a question about the platform, not about the rewrite.

    app:vxProbe is the attribute-name half, which is a different code path in a different language:
    what has to be rewritten is not the value but the resource id the attribute is looked up by, in
    the document's own attribute name map. Only an attribute belonging to this package reaches it -
    the android: ones are 0x0101xxxx and the native side skips them - so this attribute is the only
    thing in either APK that exercises that half at all.

    Both names matter, and not for where they sit in this file: aapt2 numbers the entries of a type
    in name order, so what keeps this package from numbering probe_root and vxProbe the way the
    target does is that module_only sorts ahead of probe_root and vxModuleOnly (values/attrs.xml)
    sorts ahead of vxProbe. Rename either to something sorting after and the two packages agree,
    the rewrite stops being observable, and the case reports SETUP instead of a green row.
-->
<TextView xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    android:id="@+id/probe_root"
    android:labelFor="@+id/module_only"
    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
    android:tag="REPLACED"
    android:text="replaced"
    app:vxProbe="probe" />
